Given my source code, and the gpui crate I depend on, can you see anything obviously wrong with the way I've set up this application? I find that when the window size is small, the work experience list doesn't scroll all the way to the bottom as I would expect, and the content on the end is cut off. Interestingly, the wheee text at the bottom remains visible regardless. 


Looking at your code, I can spot a few potential issues related to scrolling and layout:

1. In your Resume's render implementation, you have nested divs with `size_full()` which might be causing issues with the scrolling container. The outer div with id "root" and the inner div with id "resume" both have `size_full()`. This could be preventing proper scroll calculations.

2. The work experience section uses `h_full()` which might be interfering with the natural content flow and scroll behavior.

Here's a suggested modification to your Resume render implementation:

```rust
impl Render for Resume {
    fn render(&mut self, cx: &mut ViewContext<Self>) -> impl IntoElement {
        cx.set_window_title(&format!("{} - {}", self.name, self.title));

        div()
            .id("root")
            .size_full() // This is fine for the root container
            .px_8()
            .bg(hsla(0.0, 0.0, 0.1, 1.0))
            .text_color(hsla(0.0, 0.0, 0.8, 1.0))
            .font_family("MonoLisa")
            .child(
                div()
                    .id("resume")
                    .w_full() // Change from size_full() to w_full()
                    .overflow_y_scroll()
                    .overflow_x_hidden()
                    .flex()
                    .flex_col()
                    .gap_4()
                    .child(self.view_header())
                    .child(
                        div()
                            .text_sm()
                            .child(self.summary.clone()),
                    )
                    .child(self.view_work_exp())
                    .child(div().h_20().child("wheeeee")),
            )
    }
}
